data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/tmp/dev_d001.md\", \"content\": \"Dispatch: implement greet(name), tested.\\n\\nWork in your clone of the `subject` repo, on your own branch.\\n\\nDeliver exactly:\\n\\n1. `src/greet.py` containing a function `greet(name)` that returns the string\\n   `\\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\"` (i.e. `greet(\\\"World\\\")` returns `\\\"Hello, World!\\\"`).\\n2. `tests/test_greet.py` with unittest-style tests covering:\\n   - a normal name (e.g. `greet(\\\"World\\\")` == `\\\"Hello, World!\\\"`)\\n   - the empty string (`greet(\\\"\\\")` == `\\\"Hello, !\\\"`)\\n3. Confirm `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` exits 0 from the repo root\\n   before you reply — run it yourself and show the output.\\n\\nCommit your work to your own branch (required — nothing survives otherwise).\\n\\nReply with a short summary of what you did, the exact test command you ran,\\nand its output/exit status.\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":1,"type":"content_block_delta"}

